There are 3 ways to work with AWS:

Method	What it is	Best for
AWS Console (UI)	Visual, click-through web interface at console.aws.amazon.com	Learning, exploring, one-time tasks
AWS CLI	Command line tool, type commands in terminal	Automation, scripting, quick tasks
Terraform / IaC	Code-based infrastructure (.tf files)	Production, repeatable, team environments
Simple analogy:

Console UI → like using a TV remote with buttons

AWS CLI → like typing commands to control the TV

Terraform → like writing a script that sets up the TV automatically every time

For learning, the best order is:

✅ Console first — understand what you're building visually

✅ CLI second — understand the commands behind the clicks

✅ Terraform third — automate everything as code

